module gunbc.guarantee_stall.deployed_repository_empty_root_bootstrap_stall

import v2.std.algebra { Cons, Empty }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, ClimbableButUnbuilt, BoundedPopulation, climbs_when }

// THE CAPABILITY EXISTS NOW, AND THE CLIMB IS ONE RUNG, NOT TWO. #10722 built the Git-native
// bootstrap and proved it wet: an empty root is initialized, the candidate imported, the base ref
// created with an empty expected-old, the worktree moved by checkout -b, and the result read back
// through repository_convergence_verdict -- the same authority the ordinary path uses. #10724 made
// the publication member invoke that oneshot and nothing else, and the tree member now decides an
// absent root as an ordinary Create rather than refusing it. So this class is no longer OUTSIDE the
// ladder: the operation has a route, and it executes.
//
// IT IS MITIGATABLE AND NOT MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE, and the distinction is the enrolment of the
// evidence rather than the quality of the wall. Harm is genuinely contained at runtime: a non-empty
// root still refuses with the original pre-state cause, checkout -b refuses an existing branch, an
// empty expected-old refuses an existing ref, and the readback refuses a repository that is not at
// the candidate. What does NOT exist is a mechanism that blocks a REGRESSION: the wet witnesses
// perform host effects, so the hermetic floor refuses them at its boundary and counts them executed
// while they assert nothing. Reporting this as MechanicallyPreventable would be the rung inflation
// DESIGN 4b(1) names -- citing a wall that does not run.
//
// THE POPULATION IS ONE PRODUCTION SUBJECT, NOT A SNAPSHOT OF AN OPEN SET. There is one production
// constructor, deployment_spec_srv1, and the realization binding is global rather than a field a
// future spec can silently choose, so any later production spec inherits the same route.
data deployed_repository_empty_root_bootstrap_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "an empty deployed repository root is bootstrapped to the candidate, but nothing enrolled re-establishes that it still is",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
  blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
  population: BoundedPopulation { members: Cons { head: "gunbc.live_deploy.spec deployment_spec_srv1 at a fresh repository root", tail: Empty {} } },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "the bootstrap discriminating evidence enrolled in a lane that EXECUTES it. test.claim.repository_bootstrap_wet_witness_test proves both states by execution -- an empty root reads back as the candidate, a root holding content refuses untouched -- but it performs host effects, so the hermetic floor refuses it at the boundary and counts it executed while it asserts nothing. Until a wet lane runs those two rows, a regression in the bootstrap is caught by nothing at merge time")
}
